The test constructs `profile` as an `ObjectVar` with `_var_type=Profile` and calls `__getattr__` twice with `"score"` and `"tags"`. In `ObjectVar.__getattr__`, `self` and `name` are defined at function entry; `name` is read in the dunder check on line 312. Then `var_type` is defined on line 315 and immediately read on line 317, where it is redefined; that new `var_type` is read on lines 319 and 326. `fixed_type` is defined on line 319 and read in the branch condition on line 322. Because `Profile` is a `TypedDict`, execution enters the branch at line 326, defining `attribute_type` from `var_type` and `name`; `attribute_type` is then read in the `is None` check on line 327 and again in the return on line 332. The return on line 332 also reads `self` and `name`. Deduplicating across the two calls yields the same set of pairs.

